      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Video Script to Visual Generator — AI Automatically Places the Right Image in Each Line\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow accepts a submitted video script, retrieves the latest style instructions from Google Sheets, and asks DeepSeek to identify which script lines need visuals. It loops through each visual segment, submits image-generation jobs to Kie.ai, polls until results are ready, downloads the generated images, and uploads them to Google Drive. After all segments are processed, it aggregates the results into an annotated script and saves the updated output back to the style memory sheet.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the form trigger fields so the submitted script maps to the expected videoScript input.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and set the source/destination spreadsheet or sheet used for style memory.\n- Add valid API authentication for DeepSeek in the visual-segment HTTP request node.\n- Add valid Kie.ai API credentials in both the task creation and polling HTTP request nodes.\n- Connect Google Drive credentials and choose the folder where generated images should be uploaded.\n- Review the code and set nodes to ensure field names such as text, order, image_description, imageUrl, taskId, and activeInstructions match your form and API responses.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the style memory structure, DeepSeek prompt/instructions, Kie.ai image model parameters, polling delay, maximum retry logic, Google Drive destination folder, and the final annotated script format."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
